2. OFFICIAL LISTING AUTHORITY REQUIREMENTS
   If you operate a listing instance claiming to be the "official
   reposell listing" or using the official verification key:
   
   a) You MUST operate the official pricing policy endpoint
      (`GET /api/v1/pricing`) returning cryptographically signed
      pricing policies;
   
   b) You MUST hold and protect the official signing private key;
      the corresponding public key MUST be distributed as
      `config/reposell/verification-key.pub`;
   
   c) You MUST implement the public listing registration
      endpoint and issue valid `ListingIdentity` records;
   
   d) You MUST implement the trust document endpoint for key
      rotation with signed key metadata;
   
   e) You MUST run the official compliance validation in CI for
      all deployments (verify.yml MUST pass).

3. PROTOCOL COMPLIANCE
   Any listing implementation (official or public) MUST:
   
   a) Implement the `/listing` manifest schema as specified
      in the protocol version;
   
   b) Verify repository manifests using the official verification
      key or a key from the current trust document;
   
   c) Calculate fees according to the signed pricing policy;
      NEVER hardcode fee percentages;
   
   d) Record immutable accounting snapshots for every transaction
      including: product price, currency, listing fee,
      main listing percentage, public listing percentage,
      repository owner amount, listing amounts, pricing policy
      ID, and pricing policy version;
   
   e) Implement idempotency for all financial operations.

